  "changed": [
    "Explicit producer-bound v2 contract metadata retains v1 default behavior,source ownership,current successful source proof,policy freshness and producer authority/root checks. It creates no event or byte effect.",
    "HTTP query requires all three exact output reference fields once;unknown,incomplete,duplicate,invalid and oversized shapes refuse. CLI uses protected reference JSON. Catalog38-v16 MCP adds only an optional closed read-only output reference;no approval tool or receive-adapter dependency.",
    "Browser discovers only this producer's current supported output contracts,selects and reloads metadata,clears old review,and keeps default output selection explicit. Complete reference and session identity/root/authority are checked before and after transport. No receiving,forwarding,execution or release grant follows.",
    "Original PostgreSQL/HTTPS/stock-SDK/CLI and five-audit Chrome profiles remain. Added producer cases and a separate six-audit Chrome selection/recovery/processing/release profile to existing native CI without dropping original entries."
